        "question": "Draw the diagram of heart and explain blood circulation ?",
        "options": [],
        "answer": "na",
        "solution": "[img]\r\n\r\n1. Deoxygenated blood from various organs of the body is received by the right atrium through the superior and inferior vena cava.\r\n2. At the same time left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lung through the pulmonary veins. \r\n3. Now both the atria contract and the deoxygenated blood from right atrium is poured into right ventricle and oxygenated blood from left atrium is poured into left ventricle. \r\n4. Now both the ventricles contract. Due to contraction of right ventricle, the blood enters into lungs through arteries. \r\n5. In lungs CO₂ is released from blood and O₂ diffuses into it. While due to contraction of left ventricle, oxygenated blood is distributed to all the parts of the body through the aorta. \r\n6. The separation of both types of the blood in the heart allows a highly efficient supply of oxygen to the body. \r\n7. This is useful in the animals which have high energy need, such as birds and mammals, which constantly use energy, to maintain their body temperature.",
